#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Courses and tutorials {#courses-and-tutorials}"
msgstr "Kursus dan tutorial {#courses-and-tutorials}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommended learning material for developing quantum teams. Below are brief "
"learning outcomes and intended audiences for each learning asset. Follow the"
" links for more details on each.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahan pembelajaran yang disyorkan untuk membangunkan pasukan kuantum. Di "
"bawah adalah hasil pembelajaran ringkas dan audiens yang disasarkan untuk "
"setiap aset pembelajaran. Ikuti pautan untuk butiran lanjut tentang setiap "
"aset.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum business foundations](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):** \n"
"* Audience: Accessible to anyone. Ideal for raising awareness across the broader institution, possibly not necessary for core team.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with quantum computing terminology, the state of the science, and awareness of a few application areas and areas of potential business value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Asas perniagaan kuantum](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mudah diakses oleh sesiapa sahaja. Sesuai untuk meningkatkan kesedaran di seluruh institusi yang lebih luas, mungkin tidak perlu untuk pasukan teras.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Kebiasaan dengan terminologi pengkomputeran kuantum, keadaan sains, dan kesedaran tentang beberapa bidang aplikasi dan bidang nilai perniagaan yang berpotensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audience: Those seeking a deep theoretical foundation for quantum computing: students and early career scientists.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Theoretical foundations of classical and quantum information, ability to describe quantum systems using linear algebra, describe multi-qubit systems and entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Asas maklumat kuantum](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka yang mencari asas teori yang mendalam untuk pengkomputeran kuantum: pelajar dan saintis kerjaya awal.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Asas teori maklumat klasikal dan kuantum, keupayaan untuk menerangkan sistem kuantum menggunakan aljabar linear, menerangkan sistem berbilang Qubit dan pembelengguan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum diagonalization algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with algorithms like VQE, SQD, and SKQD, explain how different algorithms' costs scale with variables like problem size and the number of groups of commuting Pauli operators, and how to choose a good approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Algoritma pepenjuru kuantum](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka yang mempunyai latar belakang kuantum dan pengkomputeran yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Kebiasaan dengan algoritma seperti VQE, SQD, dan SKQD, menjelaskan bagaimana kos algoritma yang berbeza berskala dengan pemboleh ubah seperti saiz masalah dan bilangan kumpulan operator Pauli yang kalis tukar tertib, dan cara memilih pendekatan yang baik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these self-guided courses, many tutorials on IBM Quantum&reg;"
" Platform showcase the latest algorithms and most powerful methods. "
"Tutorials tend to be shorter assets, showing a streamlined implementation of"
" a method. Here are a few of particular interest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain kursus berpandukan diri ini, banyak tutorial di Platform IBM "
"Quantum&reg; mempamerkan algoritma terbaru dan kaedah paling berkuasa. "
"Tutorial biasanya merupakan aset yang lebih pendek, menunjukkan implementasi"
" kaedah yang diperkemas. Berikut adalah beberapa yang menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[CHSH inequality](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):** \n"
"* Audience: For users fairly new to quantum computing. \n"
"* Learning outcomes: There are quantum correlations that are stronger than classical physics can explain, familiarity running a job using Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Ketaksamaan CHSH](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):**\n"
"* Audiens: Untuk pengguna yang agak baru dalam pengkomputeran kuantum.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Terdapat korelasi kuantum yang lebih kuat daripada yang dapat dijelaskan oleh fizik klasikal, kebiasaan menjalankan kerja menggunakan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: How to use an SQD approach to find the ground state energy of a chemical system.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Pepenjuru kuantum berasaskan sampel bagi Hamiltonian kimia](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka yang mempunyai latar belakang kuantum dan pengkomputeran yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Cara menggunakan pendekatan SQD untuk mencari tenaga keadaan asas sistem kimia.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Use the Krylov method from linear algebra, combine the speed of SQD with convergence guarantees from the Krylov method, know the conditions for convergence guarantees.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Pepenjuru kuantum Krylov berasaskan sampel bagi model kekisi fermionik](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka yang mempunyai latar belakang kuantum dan pengkomputeran yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Gunakan kaedah Krylov dari aljabar linear, gabungkan kelajuan SQD dengan jaminan penumpuan dari kaedah Krylov, ketahui syarat untuk jaminan penumpuan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are many other courses and tutorials available on [IBM Quantum "
"Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/). Check it out to see all the "
"latest content!\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat banyak lagi kursus dan tutorial yang tersedia di [Platform IBM "
"Quantum](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/). Semak untuk melihat semua "
"kandungan terbaru!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Technical development best practices {#technical-development-best-practices}"
msgstr ""
"Amalan terbaik pembangunan teknikal {#technical-development-best-practices}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Follow dev/ops best practices such as CI/CD\n"
msgstr "Ikuti amalan terbaik dev/ops seperti CI/CD\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Develop incrementally, using agile methodology to scale up a technical "
"approach and project\n"
msgstr ""
"Bangunkan secara berperingkat, menggunakan metodologi agile untuk memperluas"
" pendekatan dan projek teknikal\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use simulators for debugging and benchmarking (Do not rely on simulators for"
" too long in proof-of-concept (POC) work; they will not scale to utility)\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan simulator untuk penyahpepijatan dan penanda aras (Jangan bergantung "
"pada simulator terlalu lama dalam kerja bukti konsep (POC); ia tidak akan "
"berskala ke utiliti)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reach out to [IBM Quantum Technical support](/guides/support) via the [IBM "
"Cloud Support Center](https://cloud.ibm.com/unifiedsupport/cases/form) for "
"assistance with general technical support inquiries \n"
msgstr ""
"Hubungi [Sokongan teknikal IBM Quantum](/guides/support) melalui [Pusat "
"Sokongan IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/unifiedsupport/cases/form) untuk "
"bantuan dengan pertanyaan sokongan teknikal umum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use software features such as [Qiskit addons](/guides/addons) and [Qiskit "
"Functions](/guides/functions) to fast-track technical development, learning,"
" and discovery\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan ciri perisian seperti [tambahan Qiskit](/guides/addons) dan [Fungsi "
"Qiskit](/guides/functions) untuk mempercepatkan pembangunan teknikal, "
"pembelajaran, dan penemuan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the most out of quantum computing resources**\n"
msgstr "**Dapatkan manfaat maksimum daripada sumber pengkomputeran kuantum**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computer access is a precious resource. It is important that "
"technical practitioners use their allocated QPU time, and that they use it "
"wisely. We recommend establishing expected good technical practices that "
"ensure your team is using real quantum computers, scaling problems "
"responsibly, and allocating time appropriately. \n"
msgstr ""
"Akses komputer kuantum adalah sumber yang berharga. Adalah penting bahawa "
"pengamal teknikal menggunakan masa QPU yang diperuntukkan, dan bahawa mereka"
" menggunakannya dengan bijak. Kami syorkan menetapkan amalan teknikal yang "
"baik yang dijangkakan untuk memastikan pasukan anda menggunakan komputer "
"kuantum sebenar, menskalakan masalah dengan bertanggungjawab, dan "
"memperuntukkan masa dengan sewajarnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend starting with small test problems, and increasing to the full-"
"scale problem of interest in a few steps. This is important for reasons "
"beyond resource allocation. \n"
msgstr ""
"Kami syorkan untuk bermula dengan masalah ujian kecil, dan meningkat kepada "
"masalah berskala penuh yang diminati dalam beberapa langkah. Ini penting "
"atas sebab-sebab di luar peruntukan sumber.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As IBM&reg; quantum computers are becoming more powerful, results become "
"increasingly difficult to check with classical computers. Indeed, no "
"classical simulator can exactly simulate all functionality of a modern IBM "
"quantum computer with over 100 qubits. \n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila komputer kuantum IBM&reg; menjadi semakin berkuasa, keputusan "
"menjadi semakin sukar untuk disemak dengan komputer klasikal. Sesungguhnya, "
"tiada simulator klasikal yang dapat mensimulasikan secara tepat semua fungsi"
" komputer kuantum IBM moden dengan lebih daripada 100 Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the era of useful quantum computing, the role of simulators is mostly "
"limited to debugging code. Benchmarking with smaller versions of your "
"problem is one alternative when classical confirmation is no longer "
"feasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam era pengkomputeran kuantum yang berguna, peranan simulator "
"kebanyakannya terhad kepada penyahpepijatan kod. Penanda aras dengan versi "
"masalah yang lebih kecil adalah satu alternatif apabila pengesahan klasikal "
"tidak lagi boleh dilaksanakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In many cases, the scaling of your problem may be obvious, such as scaling a"
" machine learning problem by increasing, for example, the number of data "
"points, or the number of features. Another example is the scaling of quantum"
" chemistry problems. It would be prudent for a technical practitioner to run"
" example calculations on small molecules before tackling larger, more "
"interesting systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam banyak kes, penskalaan masalah anda mungkin jelas, seperti menskalakan"
" masalah pembelajaran mesin dengan meningkatkan, misalnya, bilangan titik "
"data, atau bilangan ciri. Contoh lain adalah penskalaan masalah kimia "
"kuantum. Adalah bijak bagi pengamal teknikal untuk menjalankan pengiraan "
"contoh pada molekul kecil sebelum menangani sistem yang lebih besar dan "
"lebih menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A workflow for scaling up a quantum "
"calculations.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/standing-up-team/scaling.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Aliran kerja untuk memperluas pengiraan "
"kuantum.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/standing-up-team/scaling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next lessons, we address promoting your team's abilities to outside "
"groups. Depending on your organization, this might mean grant writing and "
"bringing in collaborators, or it might mean selling your services to "
"clients.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran seterusnya, kita membincangkan mempromosikan keupayaan "
"pasukan anda kepada kumpulan luar. Bergantung pada organisasi anda, ini "
"mungkin bermakna penulisan geran dan mendapatkan kolaborator, atau ia "
"mungkin bermakna menjual perkhidmatan anda kepada klien.\n"
